-- N3 example sentences, batch 5: half-done, hard to do, and whose fault it was.
--
-- 〜気味 and 〜かけ describe something partway; 〜がたい and 〜ようがない
-- describe something you cannot manage. 〜つつ, 〜ながらも, 〜ものの and
-- 〜くせに all concede a point before contradicting it, and the last two —
-- 〜せいで and 〜おかげで — split blame from credit for the same shape of
-- sentence, which is why they sit next to each other here.
--
-- Two rewordings:
--
--   食べかけのパンを置いた matched 食べかけのパンを as ONE token glossed
--   "to eat" — the longest-first index swallowed the whole phrase along with
--   its particle. Breaking the run with 机の上に … があります keeps the pieces
--   apart.
--
--   いい店 shreds to い|い: the index holds 良い but not the kana spelling.
--   The shop is 有名 instead.
--
-- Additive, idempotent, safe on a live database.

  -- gimi
